# Rule: Multimodal Prompts (Vision/Audio)

## Use RunnableLambda (NOT ChatPromptTemplate):
```python
from langchain_core.runnables import RunnableLambda
from langchain_core.messages import SystemMessage, HumanMessage

def format_messages(inputs: dict) -> list:
    return [
        SystemMessage(content="System prompt"),
        HumanMessage(content=[
            {"type": "image_url", "image_url": {"url": inputs["image_url"]}},
            {"type": "text", "text": inputs.get("context", "")},
        ])
    ]

chain = RunnableLambda(format_messages) | llm
```

## Critical Format:
- Image URL: `{"url": "https://..."}` (nested, not bare string)
- Pydantic models: Use `model.attribute` (NOT `model.get('attribute')`)

## Why:
`ChatPromptTemplate` can't interpolate variables in nested structures → sends literal `"{image_url}"` to API
